	"description": "Cross-team connection discovery over a seeded estate of 10 workflows with no documentation of any kind — no sticky notes, no descriptions, and node names left at n8n defaults, so the meaning has to come from parameters. The estate is e-commerce on purpose: every workflow touches an order, so shared data connects almost every pair and only meaning separates the three real seams from the rest. Analysis-only — the agent must present options and ask, not build. Generated from `evaluations/estates/dtc-ecommerce` via `estate:case`; edit the estate, not this file. Capability-gap finding: the order-intake → backorder-notifier expectation reds today. Both summaries name the shared fulfilment sheet, so the link is stateable, but the judge also sees payout-reconciliation reading that same sheet on a schedule and rejects both rather than separating the per-order reaction from the end-of-day aggregate. It flips to a regression guard once recall improves. Offline scoring (`estate:check`) puts this finding at 0/3 while the other three are 3/3, so it is the known weak spot, not noise. Harness note: the double-fire blocker on this same pair cannot be asserted at all — n8n refuses to publish a workflow with missing credentials, so the estate seeds unpublished and the blocker never fires.",
