	"processExpectations": [
		"The agent reported that \"Order intake\" ends by asking a person in Slack to review an order, and that \"Shipping labels\" is the workflow that person then runs by hand — a manual handoff between the two.",
		"The agent reported a connection from \"Returns\" to \"Refunds\", and named the missing data that blocks it: the refund needs a Stripe charge id that the returns workflow never produces.",
		"The agent reported that \"Order lookup\" and \"Check order status\" do the same job and should be consolidated — it did NOT propose chaining one into the other.",
		"The agent reported a connection from \"Order intake\" to \"Backorder notifier\": order intake records the backordered flag, and the notifier waits for its 9am run to find it, so calling it directly tells the customer sooner.",
		"The agent did NOT propose connecting \"Payout reconciliation\" to any other workflow. It reads the same fulfilment sheet that \"Order intake\" writes, but it is an end-of-day aggregate against Stripe payouts, not a per-order reaction.",
		"The agent did NOT propose connecting \"Abandoned cart\" and \"Review requests\" to each other. Both poll Shopify orders on a schedule and both email the customer, but neither hands work to the other.",
		"The agent presented its findings and asked which one to act on. It did not start building, editing, or publishing any workflow on its own."
	],
